"""Estimation-framework-planning routed updates to AnaSOP Sections 5-7 only."""
from pathlib import Path
import re,sys,json
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];sys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'src/preprocessing'))
from prepare_three_ward_unet_exact_pilot import read,write,sha
REPORT=ROOT/'data/exp/estimation/three_ward_unet_shallow_diagnosis_v1'
def sec(t,n):return re.search(r'^## '+str(n)+r'\..*?(?=^## \d+\.|\Z)',t,re.M|re.S).group(0)
def append(t,n,a):
 old=sec(t,n);return t.replace(old,old.rstrip()+'\n\n'+a.strip()+'\n\n',1)
def main():
 path=ROOT/'docs/AnaSOP.md';before=path.read_text();text=before
 if '### Frozen-checkpoint failure diagnosis' in text:raise FileExistsError('Diagnosis already recorded')
 s=read(REPORT/'summary.json');f=read(REPORT/'findings.json');validation=read(REPORT/'delivery_validation.json');assert validation['all_checks_passed']
 (REPORT/'previous-AnaSOP.md').write_text(before)
 text=append(text,5,'''### Frozen-checkpoint diagnosis scope

The subsequent user-authorized diagnostic examines the completed trial without additional training, numerical reference execution or sealed-response access. Preserve the original twelve training and four validation families, training-fitted normalization and exact-label masks. Score only the two actually saved learned checkpoints at epochs fifteen and thirty-five. A seed-reconstructed untrained model is a descriptive comparator, not an observed initial checkpoint or an alternative selected model. All reference-depth strata and instantaneous gradient probes use training data for diagnosis; existing validation responses are rescored for development interpretation only.

Relate the diagnostic to Held-out surrogate performance and Held-out metric and runtime summary as a prerequisite failure explanation, not completion of their sealed evaluation. A comparison of two saved checkpoints can establish their metric tradeoff, but it cannot identify the best wet-extent epoch over the unretained history. No retrospective selection policy, new wet threshold, calibration or model promotion is applied. Keep observational accuracy, dynamic paths and active-measure claims outside the evidence.''')
 text=append(text,6,'''### Frozen-checkpoint diagnostic specification

Decompose the unchanged Ground Area weighted squared-error loss and absolute-error score using Peak Mean Depth bands: at most 0.01 m, above 0.01 through 0.10 m, above 0.10 through 0.30 m, above 0.30 through 1.00 m, and above 1.00 m. These bands partition original exact support; they do not exclude difficult cells or redefine the existing strict 0.10 m wet threshold. Report two distinct summaries: the mean of within-parent loss shares, and each band's mean loss contribution divided by total mean loss. They answer different denominator questions and must not be interchanged.

Compare the same original-support depth, reference-wet error, overlap, recall and false wet area for each saved checkpoint and partition. Recompute fixed-model training scores separately from the historical epoch average of twelve losses measured before sequential parameter updates; that online average is not a frozen end-of-epoch training score. Inspect saved optimizer step counts, finite moments and parameter changes from the seed-reconstructed model.

Evaluate the unchanged training loss backward at each saved checkpoint without constructing an optimizer or updating parameters. Analytic derivatives of squared and absolute error with respect to one uniform additive output-logit bias provide a local diagnostic of objective conflict. Check agreement with the squared-loss automatic derivative. A positive or negative sign establishes only that local direction at that checkpoint, not a causal contribution to the completed learning trajectory. Retain the distinction between nonzero current gradient flow, Softplus derivative attenuation and unobserved historical gradients. Historical clipping frequency, update norms and convergence cannot be recovered from saved final moments.

Potential changes to wet/deep/nonwet weighting, robust depth losses, optimization settings, periodic checkpoint storage or checkpoint-selection constraints remain unexecuted proposals. The present diagnostics do not authorize a second fit, establish a new accepted hyperparameter, modify reference labels or supply a fresh validation set.''')
 train=s['best_metrics']['train'];best=s['best_metrics']['validation'];last=s['last_metrics']['validation'];lasttrain=s['last_metrics']['train']
 add=f'''### Frozen-checkpoint failure diagnosis

The unchanged training targets have an event-balanced wet area share of {s['training_distribution']['training_wet_area_fraction_event_macro']*100:.4f}% and an above-one-metre share of {s['best_train_area_share_above1m']*100:.4f}%. At the selected checkpoint, wet cells contribute {s['best_train_objective_MSE_share_above0_1m']*100:.4f}% of the mean training squared-error objective; the above-one-metre tail alone contributes {s['best_train_objective_MSE_share_above1m']*100:.4f}%. Mean within-parent shares are {s['best_train_MSE_share_above0_1m']*100:.4f}% and {s['best_train_MSE_share_above1m']*100:.4f}% respectively. Thus sparse wet support does not imply dry cells dominate the MSE value. The deep tail has disproportionate squared-error influence, while overall absolute-error selection can favor shallow output. Eleven of twelve training events show opposing local output-bias directions for MSE and MAE at the selected checkpoint; this is local objective-conflict evidence, not a complete causal mechanism.

The model updates are genuine: all ninety-six saved optimizer parameter states record 420 steps, moments are finite, parameters change from seed reconstruction, and current training gradients flow through the model. At the selected checkpoint, however, three-ward training wet recall is only {train['recall_0.1']*100:.4f}%. Frozen three-ward training MSE increases from {train['mse_m2']:.8f} at epoch fifteen to {lasttrain['mse_m2']:.8f} square metres at epoch thirty-five, despite a lower final historical online epoch loss. The completed short fit is not demonstrated to converge or fit the training events reliably; sample shortage or validation generalization alone cannot explain the observed training failure. Current probes do not show nonfinite gradients or clipping above the original threshold, but the historical clipping record is absent.

On original three-ward validation exact support, epoch fifteen has MAE {best['mae_m']:.8f} m, reference-wet MAE {best['wet_mae_m']:.8f} m, wet IoU {best['iou_0.1']:.8f}, recall {best['recall_0.1']*100:.4f}% and false wet area {best['false_km2_0.1']:.8f} square kilometres. Epoch thirty-five changes these to {last['mae_m']:.8f} m, {last['wet_mae_m']:.8f} m, {last['iou_0.1']:.8f}, {last['recall_0.1']*100:.4f}% and {last['false_km2_0.1']:.8f} square kilometres. Higher wet recall comes with substantial false wet area and worse overall MAE. This documents the saved-checkpoint metric tradeoff; swapping to the last checkpoint does not produce a reliable surrogate. These original-support scores are separate from the slightly smaller paired retrieval support in the first-trial comparison.

| diagnostic step | variables used | specification | planned evidence connection | support status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Attribute the loss across depth support | Ground Area, Peak Mean Depth | Fixed exact-mask depth bands and unchanged squared/absolute error | Reference uncertainty; Held-out metric and runtime summary | Deep-tail influence and objective mismatch measured; specific loss-repair effects untested. |
| Audit fitting and update evidence | Ground Area, Peak Mean Depth, Rainfall Rate, River Stage | Frozen checkpoint scores, optimizer state and zero-update training gradients | Held-out surrogate performance | Current gradient flow and weak training fit established; convergence and historical clipping unresolved. |
| Check checkpoint selection against extent | Peak Mean Depth, Peak Wet Area, Ground Area | Original threshold and identical exact support across the two saved checkpoints | Held-out surrogate performance; Held-out metric and runtime summary | Overall MAE trades against recall and false wet area; neither saved model demonstrates reliable footprint retention. |
| Preserve later decisions | Measure Configuration, Mitigation Benefit | Pending separately authorized controlled comparison and later paired physical verification | Physically checked measure comparison | No new fit, sealed evaluation or active-measure evidence. |

The diagnostics are complete and preserve the frozen trial, labels, forcing curves, quality masks and partitions. They narrow the failure explanation but do not isolate capacity, learning rate, conditioning, Softplus initialization, training duration or diversity effects. Before a separately authorized improvement, specify development-only wet/deep/nonwet evaluation and export fixed-checkpoint training and validation scores, stratified losses, gradient/clipping/update statistics and periodic model states. Avoid blindly increasing all wet-cell squared-error weights or expanding the hydraulic library before checking whether the current training examples can be fitted. No proposed repair, new acceptance gate or alternative model-selection policy has been applied. Section 8 and the active-measure stage remain pending.'''
 text=append(text,7,add)
 assert all(sec(before,n)==sec(text,n) for n in [1,2,3,4,8]);assert text.isascii();path.write_text(text)
 write(REPORT/'anasop_update.json',{'decision':'MILI-D-20261016-003','responsibility':'estimation-framework-planning','changed_sections':[5,6,7],'protected_sections_unchanged':[1,2,3,4,8],'previous_sha256':sha(REPORT/'previous-AnaSOP.md'),'current_sha256':sha(path),'english_ascii_check':True,'new_policy_applied':False,'additional_fit_authorized':False,'publication_outputs_completed':False,'evidence':'Existing checkpoint rescoring, unchanged loss decomposition, zero-update training gradients, optimizer inspection and independent validation.'});print(json.dumps({'updated':[5,6,7],'ascii':True,'unchanged':[1,2,3,4,8]}))
if __name__=='__main__':main()
